# Kashmiri Willow Bats — Environment Variables

# WhatsApp business number (country code, no + or spaces)
# Example: 919876543210
NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=919XXXXXXXXX

# Admin dashboard at /admin/orders — the order list, which shows customer names,
# phone numbers and addresses. Guarded by HTTP Basic in middleware.ts.
#
# With these unset the dashboard serves nothing at all (503). That is deliberate:
# it must never be open by default, because "we'll add auth later" is how a
# customer database ends up public.
#
# Choose your own password and put both in .env.local, which is git-ignored.
# Use a long random one — Basic auth sends it on every request, so only run this
# over localhost or HTTPS, never plain HTTP on a public host.
ADMIN_USER=
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ── Database (Supabase) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION. With these unset the app falls back to JSON files under
# .data/, which is fine on localhost or a self-hosted Node server and *silently
# loses every order* on Vercel, Netlify or Lambda, where the filesystem is
# discarded between requests.
#
# `POST /api/orders` refuses to take an order rather than lose one: on a host it
# recognises as ephemeral with no Supabase configured, it returns the same "send it
# to us on WhatsApp" failure the customer would see if the write had failed.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Create a project at supabase.com (pick the region nearest your customers —
#      ap-south-1 / Mumbai for India).
#   2. SQL Editor -> paste supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql -> Run.
#   3. Project Settings -> API -> copy the values below.
#
# The service-role key bypasses row-level security and can read the whole orders
# table, names and addresses included. It is NOT prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ on purpose:
# that prefix would inline it into client JavaScript. Never expose it, never commit
# it, and rotate it if it ever leaves the server.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Optional. Keys the HMAC that identifies a caller in the rate_limits table, so the
# table holds an unlinkable digest rather than a recoverable IP address. Without it
# the service-role key is used instead, which works but means rotating that key
# re-buckets any in-flight rate-limit window. Any long random string.
RATE_LIMIT_SALT=

# Future integrations (not used in homepage v1)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY=
# RAZORPAY_SECRET=
# CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
# CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
# CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=
